<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Limes Tripolitanus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">from 75 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Limes Tripolitanus was a Roman frontier zone of forts and fortified farms in Tripolitania, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, developed from about 75 CE. It protected the coastal cities and controlled movement from the desert interior. It was a response to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garamantian-empire">Garamantian Empire</a> and other Saharan peoples whom Roman campaigns never permanently subdued.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/limes-tripolitanus.jpg" alt="Limes Tripolitanus" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mediatus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Limes_Tripolitanus.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
